{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The Nephilim.</b> So named because they fell and caused the world to fall; and in the Hebrew language it is a term for giants." "<b>In those days.</b> In the days of the generation of Enosh and the sons of Cain (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And also after that.</b> Even though they saw the destruction of the generation of Enosh — when Oceanus rose and flooded a third of the world — the generation of the Flood was not humbled to learn from them." "<b>Who would come.</b> They would give birth to giants like themselves." "<b>The mighty men.</b> To rebel against the Omnipresent." "<b>The men of the Name.</b> Those who were designated by names — Irad, Mechujael, Methushael — were designated for a name of destruction, for they were blotted out and uprooted. Another interpretation: men of desolation — for they desolated the world."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:42.891678435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}